<title>BELGIUM: EU agrees on lira return to ERM - diplomats.</title>
<headline>EU agrees on lira return to ERM - diplomats.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union agreed on Sunday to allow the Italian lira to return to the EU's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM), EU diplomats said.</p>
<p>The rate of lira' entry was not immediately available.  </p>
<p>An EU official later said that the lira was likely to enter the EU's stablity grid at 990 to the mark, but that the ministers gathered at a meeting in Brussels were now getting final approval for the rate from their capitals.</p>
<p>The decision followed two days of negotiations, in which the Italians pushed for a weaker rate at 1,000 to the mark or lower.</p>
<p>But a vast majority of EU ministers and central bank heads wanted a stronger lira level, between 950 and 980 to the mark.</p>
</text>
